1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["gate_ops.py:200 `section, _manifest = completion_prefetch.assemble_prefetch(spec, ...)` — the manifest return value is bound to `_manifest` and discarded","completion_prefetch.py:190 `manifest.append({\"path\": path, \"mode\": mode})` — manifest exists only inside clamp_and_format, not on the verdict result","gate_ops.py:196 `if os.environ.get(\"REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH\") == \"0\": context = base` — the prefetch-disabled path assembles no manifest","No existing `completion_prefetch_manifest` key in the codebase (search returned no matches)"],"finding":"The fingerprint composite depends on the prefetch manifest ({path,mode}), but that manifest is currently discarded at gate_ops.py:200 (`section, _manifest = completion_prefetch.assemble_prefetch(...)`) and never reaches the verdict result; the plan asserts it is 'threaded from the precheck PRE-LOAD MANIFEST' without naming the concrete data-flow (manifest -> result key -> build_payload), and the REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH=0 branch produces no manifest at all.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f267804b92b6f89c0","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan — 'Normal pinned PASS/FAIL ... completion_prefetch_manifest identifiers (path, mode) threaded from the precheck's PRE-LOAD MANIFEST'","norm_id":"n632344557e1db80a","priority":0.469,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer wires build_payload to read result['completion_prefetch_manifest'] but nothing populates it, so pinned records silently omit the prefetch identifiers","A run with REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH=0 has no manifest, so the composite differs from a prefetch-on run of identical material — unstated whether that is intended input-identity or an accidental fingerprint mismatch"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"y